CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "mb_dh_rad1_building_height_overlay", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"max_building_height\", \"operator\": \"<=\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"value is the maximum mapped on Overlay map - Building heights for the lot\"], \"exceptions\": [\"mapped minimums do not apply to dwelling houses\", \"domestic outbuildings use RAD26\"], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Dwelling house (not domestic outbuildings)' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: YES - RAD carries note 'Non-compliance with this RAD is a planning scheme matter for which Council will exercise a concurrence agency role ...'; Table 1.6.1 identifies 9.3.1 'RADs and performance outcomes identified by notes as a planning scheme matter' as the alternative provisions to QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions (Building Act s33).\nResearcher notes: Numeric value is map-based (see rule mb_building_heights_overlay_categories). Most low-density residential land is mapped 'Max 8.5m' per council open data, but the lot-specific value must be read from the map."}$q$::jsonb);
