 - Warehouse - Wholesale nursery - Winery", "extracted_value": false, "extracted_operator": "="}, "unit": null, "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-09-11", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "MORETON_BAY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "CMB:LIMITED_DEVELOPMENT"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "mb_ld_purpose_dwelling_house_not_included", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"dwelling_house_consistent_use\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": false, \"unit\": null, \"conditions\": [\"Dwelling house is listed among the uses the zone does not include\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Dwelling house (use), which by definition includes domestic outbuildings' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: The zone 'includes' only: Outdoor sport and recreation, Cropping - where involving forestry for wood production, Park, Permanent Plantation (rule 15656). Rule 15659: 'Development not included in the tables above may be considered on its merits and where it reflects and supports the outcomes of the zone.' Purpose (rule 15655) opens: 'Identify land known to be affected by extremely unacceptable intolerable flood and/or storm tide risks which pose severe restrictions on the ability of land to be developed for urban purposes.' and 'Limit any further urban development and promote transition of existing uses away from the areas of extremely unacceptable intolerable risk.'"}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$CMB.mb_ld_purpose_dwelling_house_not_included@2026-09-11$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016@2026-09-11$q$, $q$Table 6.2.8.1 PO4$q$, 'PERFORMANCE_OUTCOME', $q$PO4 On-site landscaping is provided, that: - is incorporated into the design of the development; - does not involve fill; - does not result in loss of flood storage or changes to flow paths; - reduces the dominance of car parking and servicing areas from the street frontage; - incorporates shade trees in car parking areas; - retains mature trees wherever possible; - contributes to quality public spaces by providing shelter and shade contributing to the microclimate; - maintains the achievement of active frontages and sightlines for casual surveillance. Note - Landscaping is to be provided in accordance with Planning scheme policy - Integrated design. || No example provided.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 15671$q$, NULL, $q$6.2.8 Limited development zone code$q$, NULL, $q$https://eplan.moretonbay.qld.gov.au/planningscheme/api/l/r/114/0/false/11-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$No numeric landscape or impervious-area requirement.$q$, $q$mb_ld_po4_landscaping_no_fill$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "CMB.mb_ld_po4_landscaping_no_fill", "instrument_version": "MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016@2026-09-11", "topic": "LANDSCAPE.OPEN_SPACE", "title": "Table 6.2.8.1 PO4", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DISCRETIONARY", "provision_kind": "PERFORMANCE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_LANDSCAPE", "operator": "=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "PO4 On-site landscaping is provided, that: - is incorporated into the design of the development; - does not involve fill; - does not result in loss of flood storage or changes to flow paths; - reduces the dominance of car parking and servicing areas from the street frontage; - incorporates shade trees in car parking areas; - retains mature trees wherever possible; - contributes to quality public spaces by providing shelter and shade contributing to the microclimate; - maintains the achievement of active frontages and sightlines for casual surveillance. Note - Landscaping is to be provided in accordance with Planning scheme policy - Integrated design. || No example provided.", "extracted_value": false, "extracted_operator": "="}, "unit": null, "on_noncompliance": "ASSESS_AGAINST_PERFORMANCE_OUTCOME", "effective_from": "2026-09-11", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "MORETON_BAY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "CMB:LIMITED_DEVELOPMENT"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "mb_ld_po4_landscaping_no_fill", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"landscaping_fill_permitted\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": false, \"unit\": null, \"conditions\": [\"landscaping does not involve fill\", \"no loss of flood storage or changes to flow paths\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Assessable development generally (on-site landscaping)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: Qualitative only; PO5 (rule 15672) adds revegetation per Planning scheme policy - Integrated design. Low relevance for a Class 10a / pool siting envelope."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$CMB.mb_ld_po4_landscaping_no_fill@2026-09-11$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016@2026-09-11$q$, $q$Part 1 Table 1.6.1 (rules 245, 248) read with 6.2.8 (no concurrence agency issues table)$q$, 'OTHER', $q$Alternative provisions to QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions for a dwelling house, including a class 10 building or structure. (Building Act 1975 section 33) || Section 6.2.10 Rural zone code Section 6.2.11 Rural residential zone code Section 9.3.1 Dwelling house code - RADs and performance outcomes identified by 'notes' as a "planning scheme matter". || Under schedule 9 of the Planning Regulation 2017, Council has a role as a concurrence agency for particular applications for building work made assessable under the Building Act 1975. Where this concurrence role applies, non-compliance with a “requirement for accepted development” (RAD) will not trigger a code assessable application to Council for assessment against the planning scheme. Instead, the matter will be assessed through the concurrence process. In some instances, this planning scheme uses that concurrence agency role as a replacement for triggering assessable development. However, that is limited to those instances where the relevant tables in section 5.5 allocate “accepted development” as the category of development, and prescribed applicable “requirements for accepted development” (RADs) in column 3 of the table, but compliance with one or more of the “concurrence agency issues” identified in the applicable RADs were not satisfied by the particular proposal. - Concurrence agency issues within the planning scheme are identified in “concurrence agency issues for building work” tables and by ‘notes’ within the following planning scheme codes: - Section 6.2.3 - Emerging community zone code - Section 6.2.10 - Rural zone code - Section 6.2.11 - Rural Residential zone code - Section 6.2.12 - Township zone code - Section 9.3.1 - Dwelling house code$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$rule 245, rule 248$q$, NULL, $q$6.2.8 Limited development zone code$q$, NULL, $q$https://eplan.moretonbay.qld.gov.au/planningscheme/api/l/r/15/0/false/11-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$$q$, $q$mb_ld_no_qdc_alternative_provisions$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "CMB.mb_ld_no_qdc_alternative_provisions", "instrument_version": "MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016@2026-09-11", "topic": "OTHER", "title": "Part 1 Table 1.6.1 (rules 245, 248) read with 6.2.8 (no concurrence agency issues table)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "OTHER", "measurement": "SCHEME_OTHER", "operator": "=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "Alternative provisions to QDC boundary clearance and site cover provisions for a dwelling house, including a class 10 building or structure. (Building Act 1975 section 33) || Section 6.2.10 Rural zone code Section 6.2.11 Rural residential zone code Section 9.3.1 Dwelling house code - RADs and performance outcomes identified by 'notes' as a \"planning scheme matter\". || Under schedule 9 of the Planning Regulation 2017, Council has a role as a concurrence agency for particular applications for building work made assessable under the Building Act 1975. Where this concurrence role applies, non-compliance with a “requirement for accepted development” (RAD) will not trigger a code assessable application to Council for assessment against the planning scheme. Instead, the matter will be assessed through the concurrence process. In some instances, this planning scheme uses that concurrence agency role as a replacement for triggering assessable development. However, that is limited to those instances where the relevant tables in section 5.5 allocate “accepted development” as the category of development, and prescribed applicable “requirements for accepted development” (RADs) in column 3 of the table, but compliance with one or more of the “concurrence agency issues” identified in the applicable RADs were not satisfied by the particular proposal. - Concurrence agency issues within the planning scheme are identified in “concurrence agency issues for building work” tables and by ‘notes’ within the following planning scheme codes: - Section 6.2.3 - Emerging community zone code - Section 6.2.10 - Rural zone code - Section 6.2.11 - Rural Residential zone code - Section 6.2.12 - Township zone code - Section 9.3.1 - Dwelling house code", "extracted_value": [], "extracted_operator": "in"}, "unit": null, "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-09-11", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "MORETON_BAY"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "CMB:LIMITED_DEVELOPMENT"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "mb_ld_no_qdc_alternative_provisions", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"concurrence_agency_rads\", \"operator\": \"in\", \"value\": [], \"unit\": null, \"conditions\": [\"6.2.8 is not listed as containing alternative provisions to the QDC, QDC performance-criteria provisions, amenity and aesthetics provisions, or concurrence agency issues\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Building work for a dwelling house, including a class 10 building or structure' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO - Table 1.6.1 lists only 6.2.10, 6.2.11 and 9.3.1 (rules 245, 246) and 6.2.10, 6.2.11 (rule 247); rule 248 lists 6.2.3, 6.2.10, 6.2.11, 6.2.12, 9.3.1. 6.2.8 contains no RADs at all.\nResearcher notes: There is no Council concurrence-agency pathway in this zone; because Table 5.7.1 makes building work impact assessable (rule 4428), a development permit for building work assessed against the whole planning scheme is needed. QDC MP1.1/1.2 boundary clearances would still apply at building assessment, but the planning permit governs siting."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$CMB.mb_ld_no_qdc_alternative_provisions@2026-09-11$q$;

INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$QHC transition: the scheme (Version 8, 11 Sep 2026) still refers to 'QDC part MP1.2' and 'standard as in QDC'. No QHC amendment was found. Confirm how Building Act/Regulation transitional provisions apply these references after the QHC commenced on 1 Sep 2026, especially the side/rear cells that say 'Refer to standard as in QDC' and the QDC mean-height method.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Alternative provisions in 9.3.1 are identified indirectly (Table 1.6.1 plus 'planning scheme matter' notes), not by an explicit 'alternative provision to QDC A1...' statement per RAD as in 6.2.11. RAD26 (outbuilding size/height/location) and RAD15 are amenity/aesthetic matters, not alternative provisions - confirm the engine's treatment.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Redcliffe Interim residential precinct: 9.3.1 RAD3 points to Table 9.3.1.3 while the local plan Part K RAD3 points to Table 7.2.1.6.3 (side/rear 1.5 m / 2 m). Which governs dwelling-house building work?$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Morayfield South (Emerging community Transition precinct): RAD3 routes it to Table 9.3.1.5, while E3.1 and the Table 9.3.1.6 heading route it to Table 9.3.1.6.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Table 9.3.1.4 heading includes 'Township zone - Residential precinct', but Table 5.7.1 assesses Township residential dwelling houses against the Township zone code (not fetched).$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Building heights overlay values come from 2022 council open data, not the Version 8 legal map; lot-specific verification is needed.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Site cover: the definition includes carports, but RAD5 excludes 'patios, balconies and other unenclosed structures'. Decide how to treat open carports.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Not fetched: 6.2.10 Rural zone code (also an alternative-provision code), 6.2.12 Township zone code, 6.2.3 Emerging community zone code, Woodfordia local plan, Planning scheme policy - Residential design.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$No swimming pool setback provisions were found in 9.3.1; RR code RAD3 excludes pools and refers to the QDC.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Rural residential: RAD3 (6 m / 4.5 m / 4.5 m) vs RAD48 (6 m road, 1.5-4 m by wall height) - RAD48 is specific to dwelling houses and outbuildings; confirm RAD3 does not also apply.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Rural zone (outside Hamlet): RAD3 setbacks (6m road / 4.5m side / 4.5m rear) expressly exclude 'a dwelling house', and the code has no other boundary setback RAD for a dwelling house, so the accepted-development pathway seems to leave dwelling boundary clearance to the QDC/QHC. Does RAD3 apply to domestic outbuildings, given the Dwelling house definition includes domestic outbuildings? Part B E4.1 (assessable) has no exclusion.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Rural zone: no site cover or roofed-area limit for a dwelling house or outbuildings (unlike Rural residential RAD6). Outbuilding size is unlimited by the zone code; outbuilding height = mapped building height (open data Max 8.5m) except 3.5m in the Hamlet precinct.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Township residential RAD3 rear column says 'Refer to standards in QDC' but Part F E4 says rear 6.0m. Which governs for assessable cases, and how does 'standards in QDC' read after the QHC replaced MP1.2 on 1 Sep 2026?$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Township residential: the zone code notes call RAD3 and RAD59(b)(c) 'an alternative provision to the QDC', but Table 1.6.1 (rules 245/246) lists only 6.2.10, 6.2.11 and 9.3.1 as alternative-provision codes; s1.6 rule 248 lists 6.2.12 only as having 'concurrence agency issues'. Is the Building Act s33 status of 6.2.12 provisions effective?$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Township residential RAD4 site cover (50%) and RAD1 height have no alternative-provision note, so exceeding them seems to trigger limited code assessment rather than concurrence. Confirm.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Table 5.7.1 rule 4425 editor's-note RAD lists for the Rural zone and Township residential precinct do not match current RAD numbering (e.g. Township list omits RAD59 outbuildings; Rural list omits RAD3/RAD4/RAD39). The Rural MCU table note says '(numbering needs to be checked after changes made)'. The engine should apply the zone code RADs as written.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Building heights overlay values are from 2022 council open data (sampled, not exhaustive), not the Version 8 legal map. Some Rural parcels had no polygon; check each lot.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$RAD59 outbuilding roofed-area bands: '600m2 - 1000m2' then '>1000m2 - 2000m2'; E64 header says 'Max. GFA' instead of roofed area. Treated as roofed area per RAD59.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Open carports and site cover: Schedule 1 site cover includes carports, but RAD4 excludes 'other unenclosed structures'.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$No swimming pool siting provisions exist in either code; pools appear only as fire-fighting water sources in the bushfire RADs. Pool siting falls to the QDC/QHC and the pool safety standard.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$No built-to-boundary provisions in either zone. In Township residential the side minimum (1.5m/2m) applies 'To OMP and wall'.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Dwelling houses in the Township centre/convenience precincts (not listed -> impact assessment) and the Township industry precinct (inconsistent use) have no siting rules; out of scope for the tool.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Rural RAD3 refers to 'not located in a bushfire prone area' and its note to the 'bushfire hazard area'; how this carve-out maps to the Bushfire hazard overlay is not stated.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$No 'constrained land', 'Burpengary East' or any other precinct exists for this zone in V8: no child sections under 5.5.8 / 6.2.8 in the eScheme TOC, and ZONE_PREC is always empty in the zone open data. In V8 the Limited development zone is the flood/storm-tide 'extremely unacceptable intolerable risk' zone.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$No numeric siting provisions (setbacks, built-to-boundary, site cover, height, outbuilding size, pool setbacks, development footprint, lot-size conditions) exist in 6.2.8. Siting is decided case by case through impact assessment against the whole planning scheme (overlay codes such as 8.2.2 Flood hazard would drive floor levels and siting).$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Whether a swimming pool (no GFA) counts as 'minor building work' or a 'new building' under PO1 is not stated; PO1 is in any case only an impact-assessment benchmark.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$Existing lawful dwelling houses in the zone: any building work, including a new shed, carport or pool, still needs an impact-assessable application (rule 4428). The tool should flag the lot rather than compute an envelope.$q$);
INSERT INTO open_issues (lg_id, instrument_id, severity, description) VALUES ($q$MORETON_BAY$q$, $q$MBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2016$q$, 'MEDIUM', $q$The zone open-data layer has an undocumented field LDZ_DoesNotApply (all 0 for Limited development features).$q$);
